{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788975191,"nonce":"Fzf1jFqjWSXdrpUqXe3W3kdLuL0=","message":"Implemented on branch `worktree-agent-a16c11b600b062b42` — `24904bb` (feat) + `2804b10` (Build), on top of `1765ba9`. `Source/AutoRimmer/InteractableSafe.cs` (the chain, the route table) + `InteractVerbs.cs` (the two verbs), shaped as siblings of `UsableSafe.cs`/`UseVerbs.cs`. Release, 0 warnings. Acceptance is `accept/70c1f9e-interact.md`; the reasoning is in DESIGN's decisions log.\n\n## What the filing got right\n\n- `CompAnalyzable : CompInteractable` and the chips are `CompAnalyzableUnlockResearch`. Confirmed.\n- The two forbidden clauses ARE separate, DO name different strings, and ARE both skipped on `Drafted` or `Props.ignoreForbidden`. Confirmed, and they are genuinely different questions: `IntVec3.IsForbidden(Pawn)` is the allowed-area test, `Thing.IsForbidden(Pawn)` is the forbid flag. Two gates, `outside-allowed-area` and `forbidden`, and both escapes ride on the refusal row.\n- The `activateStat` clause IS one clause with two tests — the stat, then any `statFactors` entry. One gate, with the offending stat named because the game's \"Incapable\" does not name it.\n- No WorkGiver for `JobDefOf.AnalyzeItem` exists. Confirmed by grep: the only producers are `CompAnalyzable.OrderForceTarget` and the DEV gizmo.\n- The two calls do not ask the same question. Confirmed — see the correction below for *why*.\n\n## Four corrections\n\n**1. There is no `TryInteract`.** The re-checking method is `CompInteractable.Interact(Pawn caster, bool force = false)`, and it runs in the LAST toil of `JobDriver_InteractThing`, not at order time. The reason it drops `checkOptionalItems` is mechanical, not a second opinion: the toil immediately above it does `pawn.carryTracker.DestroyCarriedThing()`, so the optional item is already spent and an optional-item check would refuse the interaction it was carried for. Only `CompObeliskDeactivationInteractor` and `CompGoldenCube` read the parameter, both for Shards; the base method ignores it entirely. Modelled as its own concept — `Refusals` takes it, and `optional_items` publishes BOTH passes for a type that actually reads it.\n\n**2. \"and more past line 206\" is exactly two clauses**, and the first inverts a ruling `use` made: `!activateBy.health.capacities.CapableOf(Manipulation)` -\u003e \"MessageIncapableOfManipulation\", then `!activateBy.CanReach(parent.SpawnedParentOrMe, ClosestTouch, Deadly)` -\u003e \"CannotReach\". On `CompUsable` manipulation is an ADVISORY because the check lives inside `JobDriver_UseItem` while the float-menu provider's `RequiresManipulation` is false. Here it is IN `CanInteract`, so the game's own option is disabled and so is ours. Seventeen clauses ship: twelve base, four `CompAnalyzable` (`already-analyzed`, `research-speed`, and the bench clause in its two forms), one `CompAnalyzableUnlockResearch` (`mechanitor`).\n\n**3. Clause 3's message is `refuelable.Props.outOfFuelMessage`** — off the REFUELABLE's props. `CompProperties_Interactable` has no `outOfFuelMessage` field.\n\n**4. There is no overlap with `826d4bf`, and no `target` argument is possible.** `CompInteractable.OrderForceTarget(LocalTargetInfo target)` does `target.Pawn.jobs.TryTakeOrderedJob(...)`; `ValidateTarget` refuses `target.Pawn == null`; `OnGUI`'s cursor label is `\"ChooseWhoShouldActivate\"` (the chips override it to \"Choose who should analyze this\"). The ITargetingSource target IS THE ACTIVATING PAWN, so `interact {pawn, thing}` is already the targeted form. A stray `target` key is REFUSED pre-mutation with that said out loud, because a caller reading this issue would supply one. The real second-targeter cases are `CompNociosphere` (a destination cell) and `CompInteractableRocketswarmLauncher` (the turret's attack target), and both are refused by ROUTE.\n\n## The thing the filing did not ask about, and it is the big one\n\n`OrderForceTarget` is virtual and SEVEN vanilla classes override it, so \"make an InteractThing job\" is one route among several. The route is selected off the DECLARING TYPE of the override by reflection — not a class-name string, so a modded `CompAnalyzable` subclass that does not re-override still analyses. Two are driven: the base (`JobDefOf.InteractThing`) and `CompAnalyzable`'s (`JobDefOf.AnalyzeItem`, bench as TargetB and its cell as TargetC). The other six are refused with gate `unsupported-route` and a per-class reason read off their source — `CompGoldenCube` opens a `Dialog_MessageBox` (the `d318d4a` wedge exactly), two arm `Find.Targeter`, `CompObeliskDeactivationInteractor` hauls Shards with `job.interactableIndex = 1`, and `CompLabyrinthDoor`/`CompDisableUnnaturalCorpse` gate their float menu on a class-specific widget precondition not verified in play.\n\nAlso: a thing with MORE THAN ONE `CompInteractable` is refused (`ambiguous-interactable`), not silently resolved to the first. The void obelisk carries two and vanilla tells them apart by which gizmo was clicked.\n\n## The modal question, answered\n\nNeither driven route calls `Find.WindowStack.Add` — checked, not assumed. But `CompAnalyzable.OnAnalyzed` ends in `Find.LetterStack.ReceiveLetter`, so the advance that COMPLETES the analysis halts on **news**, not dialog. Published as `advance_halt` on the order reply. The orchestrator wants `through_news` on the advances in phase 4.\n\n## The un-forbid is AFTER the gate, unlike `use`\n\n`CompAnalyzable.OrderForceTarget` clears `CompForbiddable` only after `ValidateTarget` passed, so a forbidden chip and an undrafted pawn is a refusal the player gets too. `UsableSafe` un-forbids BEFORE ordering because its chain has no forbidden clause at all; copying that here would fabricate a permission. **Practical consequence for the run: if the bought `SignalChip` is forbidden, `unforbid {thing:\u003cid\u003e}` or draft the mechanitor first.**\n\n## Acceptance clauses I could not discharge, and why\n\n- **`on-cooldown` is not reachable on a chip.** `CompProperties_CompAnalyzableUnlockResearch` leaves `cooldownTicks` at 0, so `StartCooldown` sets 0 and `OnCooldown` is never true. The gate is implemented and tested against `Turret_FoamTurret` (`cooldownTicks: 3600`) in the acceptance doc instead.\n- **`no-power` is not reachable on a vanilla bench at all.** No shipped `CompProperties_Interactable` sets `requiresPower: true` — `GravshipShieldGenerator` sets it explicitly false. The clause is implemented and gated correctly on `Props.requiresPower` (an interactable with a `CompPowerTrader` but the flag false must NOT be refused), and `requires_power` is published on every row. Flagged rather than faked.\n- **No bench, and a worker may not launch one.** Everything above is source-verified; nothing is play-verified.\n\nFiled `55b2c6c` (p3) for a `dev:analyze` escape — the game has a \"DEV: Finish analysis\" gizmo and `AnalysisManager.ForceCompleteAnalysisProgress` is public, and the acceptance chain otherwise costs ~1250 ticks plus two walks per chip. It is `dev:*`, deliberately not folded into `interact`.","files":null}]}